.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH g-hooks 1  "g-hooks " 
.SH NAME
g\-hooks \- Manage personal git hooks
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBg\-hooks\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage personal git hooks
.PP
Configure and run personal hooks that coexist with team hooks (like Husky). Hooks are stored in .g/hooks.toml (gitignored) or ~/.config/g/hooks/.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
g\-hooks\-list(1)
List all configured hooks for this repository
.TP
g\-hooks\-run(1)
Run a specific hook manually
.TP
g\-hooks\-init(1)
Create a hooks.toml template in .g/
.TP
g\-hooks\-status(1)
Show where hooks config is loaded from
.TP
g\-hooks\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
